sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: `orbit proof COMMAND`, the first step of stage 3 of the command development pipeline. The author proves one command in the task copy they work in, with the nested fleet that copy already has and no new copy. The Gateway records the intent and the verdicts; Orbit's own Swamp reaches the copy through its Node and runs the runner in it as `agent`, restores `base` first and leaves a clean fleet after. `proof:run` is the CI path.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: proof
  %% kind: proof.verify
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane CP icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as Operator<br/>orbit proof
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant CP as Task copy<br/>agent in the copy
  CLI->>GW: Prove the command<br/>proof COMMAND --group
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the route needs Gateway access, which no copy holds; a Node with Gateway access names the group
  %%> - the cases come from the copy's own checkout, so they run against the code the author has now, committed or not
  Note over GW: Admit the proof<br/>copy · group · inputs
  %%> What it records:
  %%> - the copy's Incus project and container, its Node as the SSH target and the cases file; no secret, and no step calls back
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a group without a copy, a copy that is not active or not running, a Project without a nested fleet, a copy turn that may still run, or another operation on the group
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>operation ID
  GW->>SW: Start the run<br/>proof-fleet-verify
  SW->>CP: Select the cases<br/>runner plan --lines
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - every runner call goes Node SSH, `incus exec` into the copy, `runuser -u agent`, as a copy turn does; a missing or invalid cases file fails the run here, before the fleet changes
  SW->>CP: Restore the base snapshot<br/>first · 45 s limit
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the author's fleet may have moved since the copy started
  loop each batch, in the order of swamp/proof/batches.yaml
    SW->>CP: Run the batch<br/>restore · setup · cases
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - one restore of `base` per batch but the first, the batch start state, then each case with its own resources and no undo
  end
  SW->>CP: Restore base<br/>last · clean fleet
  %%> When:
  %%> - also after a failed case or a stopped run; a cancelled run leaves the fleet as it is
  Note over SW: Join the verdicts<br/>report step
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one line a case, in plan order; a case of a batch that did not run is `unrun` with cause `infrastructure`
  alt every case passes and the last restore succeeded
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>verdict per case
    Note over GW: Record the result once<br/>PASS
    GW-->>CLI: PASS per case<br/>timings
  else a case failed or did not run, or the last restore failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>verdict per case
    Note over GW: Record the result once<br/>FAIL
    GW--xCLI: Failed check per case<br/>exit nonzero
    %%> Result:
    %%> - `proof.cases_failed`, `proof.run_failed` or `proof.restore_failed`; the receipt of each case stays in the copy's evidence directory
  end
